=== ntfsfallocate ===
DESCRIPTION ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/usr/bin/ntfsfallocate v2022.10.3 (libntfs-3g) Copyright (c) 2013-2014
Jean-Pierre Andre Allocate clusters to a specified attribute of a specified
file.

Developers' email address: ntfs-3g-devel@lists.sf.net News, support and
information: https://github.com/tuxera/ntfs-3g/


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  ntfsfallocate [options] -l length device file [attr-type [attr-name]]


POSITIONALS (2) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  attr-type
  attr-name


FLAGS (8) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-f         Force execution despite errors
-n         Do not change the apparent size of file
-l length  Allocate length bytes
-o offset  Start allocating at offset
-v         Verbose execution
    -vv    Very verbose execution
-V         Display version information
-h         Display this help
